   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Deciding to do something",
     "texto": [
      "**-기로 하다** expresses a decision or agreement to do something: 가다 → **가기로 했어요** (I decided / we decided to go), 먹다 → **먹기로 했어요** (I decided / we decided to eat), 하다 → **하기로 했어요**. The form with 했어요 places the decision before the present moment; who the subject is and whether the decision was individual or collective is understood from the context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Earlier decision and commitment",
     "texto": [
      "**-기로 했어요** reports a decision already made, individual or shared: **친구하고 만나기로 했어요** (I arranged to meet a friend). **-(으)ㄹ게요** usually communicates the speaker's commitment or willingness towards the listener: **제가 전화할게요** (I'll call you)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
